      <h2 id="allowed">What can you do yourself?</h2>
      <p>In Spain you can do a lot yourself as an owner, but the town hall wants to know what you are doing. Broadly there are three kinds of work:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Maintenance</strong>, such as painting, limewashing, replacing a tap or putting back a tile: no notification needed.</li>
        <li><strong>Minor works</strong> (<em>obra menor</em>), such as replacing windows, renewing a bathroom or repairing the roof with the same materials: usually a notification (<em>declaración responsable</em>) or a simple permit.</li>
        <li><strong>Major works</strong> (<em>obra mayor</em>), such as a pool, an extension or anything structural: a building permit with a project by an architect.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If your house has AFO status or no full licence, you are often only allowed to do maintenance. Read our guide to <a href="/en/guides/afo-legalisation-andalusia/">AFO and legalisation</a> first. Electrics, gas and asbestos are never DIY jobs: an authorised installer or company is required by law.</p>

      <h2 id="buy">Where to buy materials</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>DIY stores</strong>: the big chains are in and around Málaga, such as Leroy Merlin and Bauhaus. Handy for tools, bathroom fittings and standard sizes.</li>
        <li><strong>Builders’ merchants</strong> (<em>almacén de materiales de construcción</em>): in Vélez-Málaga, Torre del Mar, Nerja and larger villages. For cement, lime, blocks, roof tiles and floor tiles, and they deliver with small lorries right into the villages.</li>
        <li><strong>Hardware shops</strong> (<em>ferretería</em>): in almost every village, for small items and often good advice.</li>
        <li><strong>Specialist shops</strong>: a <em>carpintería de aluminio</em> for made-to-measure windows, a <em>tienda de piscinas</em> for pool equipment, a stove shop for stoves and flues.</li>
        <li><strong>Hire</strong> (<em>alquiler de maquinaria</em>): for a mini digger, scaffolding or a cement mixer.</li>
      </ul>

