      <h2 id="pro">When to call a professional</h2>
      <p>A good rule of thumb: anything that touches the structure, electrics and gas, work at height and jobs where a mistake only shows later (waterproofing, pipes in the wall) are better left to a professional. And if you are only in Spain a few weeks a year, a job you cannot finish often ends up costing more than having it done straight away. Many owners choose a middle way: the professional does the heavy work, you do the finishing.</p>
      <p class="note">These guides give general information. You carry out the work at your own risk; if in doubt, always ask the town hall or a professional.</p>
